  "summary": "Degraded secret zeroization capabilities",
  "details": "In version 0.11.1 and earlier of vodozemac, the Olm root key ratchet did not\nzeroize its HKDF output after use. Each ratchet step left a copy of the new root\nkey and chain key in freed heap memory.\n\n## Impact\n\nAn attacker who can read the process's memory, for example through a separate\nmemory-disclosure bug, a core dump, or swapped-out pages, may recover root keys\nand chain keys from earlier ratchet steps. A leaked chain key allows decrypting\nthe messages in that chain, weakening Olm's forward secrecy for affected\nsessions.",
